claim='''\n\n## Proper-motion response extension\n\nOwner: manuscript/obsstat response; HTT conditional Gaussian design. Claim tier C0 CONDITIONAL; transfer source none (first-order kinematic response).\n\n| Claim | Source | Status and limits |\n|---|---|---|\n| Signed endpoint–derivative response, nearby positive sign | retained Marcori arXiv:1805.12121v1 Eq. 5.13 and frozen author text, equations 28–30 | DERIVED under weak homogeneous fixed-axis, comoving, nonrotating-frame assumptions; no dynamics |\n| Full five STF field and ten-coordinate history image | pm_history_supplement.json: response, history_images, history_family_q_equals_s | CONDITIONAL kinematic domain; five null directions; common-endpoint gauge distinct |\n| Same-data six versus 97 nuisance profiles | pm_history_supplement.json: gram.primary_spin_glide6 and gram.all97_sensitivity | CONDITIONAL selected optical field; full covariance and cross covariance retained |\n| Gaussian power, equations 34–35, figures 4–5 | pm_history_supplement.json: power_frontier; NUMBER_FIGURE_MAP.json; copied sealed figures | CONDITIONAL design sensitivity, not empirical significance or a shear exclusion |\n\nFull five-dimensional coefficients, all covariances, history arrays and eigenbases remain in report/pm_history_supplement.json. Exact source hashes are in SOURCE_CONTRACT.json. Unknown spatial covariance, source selection, distance/history law, optical-centroid transfer and frame calibration block an empirical matter-shear interpretation. Physical x,Q,F,Pi,G_F, vorticity and family identity remain unevaluated.\n'''
